  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Gun metal is used for making guns and is also known as red brass. Gun metals are resistant to corrosion that is caused by steam and salt water. That&rsquo;s why their composition includes metals which provides resistance to corrosion. Usually, gun metal is a type of bronze which is an alloy of copper, tin and zinc.</p><p>The major components in &quot;Gun Metal&quot; are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>87</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>",
